tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-216-a-backslash-in-a-header-name.hero:34:8: error[escape_in_header_name]: this header's name holds `\`, which clang reads in a header's name as escaping the character after it, and at the name's end that is the `>` closing it, so clang reads on into another header or none, and it names a path from a root, where this machine keeps the header rather than what the machine has
